Done — that's the Intel 82801AA AC'97 (8086:2415) at 00:04.0, which had no driver. I brought the codec up at 48 kHz stereo, installed a play driver that points its PCM-out DMA engine at the kernel's sample buffer, and you just heard a 440 Hz A for 600 ms. audio_tone and audio_melody now work; note the sink lives in RAM and is gone on the next reboot.

